+# Audit 2026-10-28 — TOML BOM Wedge (F-T1) & TOML-Validity Gate Gap (G-T3)
+
+**Cycle:** zai-cron-agent-loop Job 478318, 04:10 dispatch, auditor cadence role.
+**Base:** live `origin/main` @ `647928b` (rebased 0 behind at work-start and pre-submit).
+**Scope:** dead code, compliance drift, CI-gate proposal — per the auditor mandate.
+**Method:** full 3-tier sweep of live main, then targeted byte-level hygiene probes on
+config surfaces the existing guards do not cover.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Executive summary
+
+| ID | Finding | Severity | Disposition |
+|----|---------|----------|-------------|
+| F-T1 | Root `ruff.toml` carries a UTF-8 BOM (`EF BB BF`); stdlib `tomllib` — the repo's TOML parser of record — hard-fails on it (`TOMLDecodeError: Invalid statement (at line 1, column 1)`). | Medium (latent wedge, invisible to ruff) | **Fixed in this change set** (3-byte strip) |
+| G-T3 | No tier anywhere in the verify chain validates TOML: loop `--verify-only` has no TOML tier (8 tiers cover JSON/YAML only), `contract_parity_guard.py` byte-hygiene covers mirrored contract files only, ruff silently strips a leading BOM so it cannot catch its own config's corruption. | Gate gap | **Closed in this change set** — `tests/test_toml_validity.py` |
+| U-T1 | Upstream health confirmed: after #1590 landed, the CRLF phantom-dirty wedge is dead in the wild (fresh status clean, `tenant.tools.ts` is `i/lf w/lf`); 16 new commits re-verified: `--verify-only` 8/8 PASS, full pytest 875→877 passed / 3 skipped (incl. new #1598 dead-import ratchet 3/3 and #1600 instruction-builder fossil 12/12), boundary clean, repo-wide `git grep -Il CR` empty. | Info | No action |
+
+F-T1 is the same defect class as the CRLF wedge fixed in `docs/AUDIT_2026-10-28.md`
+(#1590): an environment-hygiene wedge that poisons agent tooling, produced no test
+failure, and was invisible to every CI gate at landing time.
+
+---
+
+## 2. F-T1 — evidence (reproduced on live main `647928b`)
+
+```text
+$ od -An -tx1 -N3 ruff.toml
+ ef bb bf                                  ← UTF-8 BOM, 3 bytes
+
+$ python3 -c "import tomllib; tomllib.load(open('ruff.toml','rb'))"
+TOMLDecodeError: Invalid statement (at line 1, column 1)   ← HARD FAIL
+
+$ repo-wide tomllib sweep (10 tracked *.toml)
+9 parsed clean — ruff.toml is the ONLY corrupt file
+
+$ ruff check --config ruff.toml --select E9,F63,F7,F82 …
+All checks passed!                         ← ruff 0.17.3 strips BOM silently (blind spot)
+```
+
+**Provenance:** `git log --follow -- ruff.toml` — the BOM entered with bridge landing
+`9c7d30c` (#1465, 2026-10-27 lineage); it is not part of the file's original #2469-era
+content.
+
+**Impact chain:**
+
+1. Any stdlib-based consumer of the lint config fails today. The repo's own ops
+   tooling standardizes on `tomllib` (`scripts/ops/advanced_analysis/*.py`); an agent
+   extending that tooling to read `ruff.toml` (the natural next step for lint-drift
+   audits, e.g. extending the #1598 dead-import work) hits a hard, cryptic failure.
+2. Editor/LSP consumers built on strict parsers (e.g. taplo family) flag line 1 as
+   invalid — human contributors see phantom red squiggles on a "working" config.
+3. The failure is silent for the tool that owns the file: ruff strips the BOM before
+   parsing, so CI's Step-1 ruff run (`deploy_preflight_guard.py` → `ruff check
+   --select=E9,F63,F7,F82 gateway core`) stays green. A config that is valid for one
+   consumer and invalid for the reference parser is a parser-tolerance split-brain —
+   exactly the drift class the byte-hygiene guards exist to prevent.
+
+## 3. Fix applied (smallest safe superior replacement)
+
+Strip the 3 BOM bytes from `ruff.toml`. Content is otherwise byte-identical.
+
+- **Post-fix proof:** `tomllib` parses it; `ruff check --select=E9,F63,F7,F82
+  gateway core` unchanged ("All checks passed!"); `git diff` shows exactly one line
+  changed (the BOM is invisible in text form — `-﻿[lint.per-file-ignores]` →
+  `+[lint.per-file-ignores]`).
+- **Boundary:** `ruff.toml` is an `APPROVED_ROOT_FILE` per
+  `scripts/ci/boundary_sanitization_guard.py:108`; not a protected path; zero
+  satellite code touched.
+
+## 4. G-T3 — the gate gap and its closure
+
+Nothing in the repo validates TOML today:
+
+| Tier | TOML coverage |
+|------|---------------|
+| `continuous_agent_loop.py --verify-only` (8 tiers) | JSON validity, YAML validity — no TOML tier |
+| `contract_parity_guard.py --check` | strict-LF + AST on mirrored contract files only |
+| `deploy_preflight_guard.py --step1-syntax` | `ruff check` (BOM-tolerant) + py_compile |
+| `binary_guard` | rejects binaries; a BOM is text — passes |
+
+**Closure:** `tests/test_toml_validity.py` (stdlib-only, offline):
+
+1. `test_repo_tracks_at_least_one_toml` — pins the gate's own wiring (and keeps
+   `ruff.toml` under F-T1 regression watch).
+2. `test_every_tracked_toml_parses_with_stdlib_tomllib` — enumerates
+   `git ls-files '*.toml'` (auto-covers future TOMLs; no allowlist to shrink),
+   asserts no UTF-8 BOM with an **actionable** message (tomllib's own BOM error
+   names neither cause nor cure — that is how F-T1 survived landing), then parses
+   each file with `tomllib`.
+
+Enforcement tier: the `tests/` registry is the repo's de-facto gate surface for the
+agent 3-tier verify ("`--verify-only` + tests" is mandated by the contribution
+pipeline), the same tier where #1598 (`test_dead_import_drift.py`) and #1600
+(`test_instruction_builder.py`) landed their gates. `.github/` is a protected path
+and is not touched.
+
+## 5. Verification (3-tier, post-rebase on `647928b`, 0 behind)
+
+```text
+[T1 Reflection]   this document, §6 (why + alternatives_rejected)
+[T2 Smoke]        continuous_agent_loop.py --verify-only → 8/8 PASS, single
+                  CONTRACT_VERSION=agent-loop-contract/1 marker
+[T3 Tests]        full pytest tests/ → 877 passed, 3 skipped (875 baseline + 2 new)
+                  spot: test_toml_validity 2/2 · test_dead_import_drift 3/3 ·
+                  test_instruction_builder 12/12 · test_ci_guards green
+[Patch proof]     od: BOM present before, absent after; tomllib FAIL→PASS;
+                  negative control: re-adding BOM to a scratch copy is rejected by
+                  tomllib (the gate would flag it)
+[Rebase]          origin/main advanced 0b018ba→647928b mid-audit; rebased, gates re-run green
+```
+
+## 6. Reflection Evidence
+
+**Why:** a tracked config file that the reference stdlib parser cannot read is a
+latent wedge for every agent and a live phantom-error for strict editors; it landed
+because no tier parses TOML. Fixing the byte without adding the tier would invite the
+next BOM; adding the tier without fixing the byte would fail the new gate on landing.
+Both ship together, 3 bytes + 1 offline test file + this report.
+
+**alternatives_rejected:**
+
+1. *Keep BOM, wrap all consumers in BOM-stripping* — spreads the workaround into
+   every future reader; violates Superior Replacement (appease the legacy byte).
+2. *Add a TOML tier to the loop's 8-tier verify chain* — touches the dispatch-critical
+   loop surface; the tests/ gate achieves enforcement without that blast radius
+   (precedent: #1598, #1600).
+3. *Convert the repo to pyproject.toml lint config* — large migration, zero added
+   correctness over the 3-byte fix.
+4. *Extend `contract_parity_guard.py` byte-hygiene to all TOMLs* — mixes concerns in
+   a guard scoped to mirrored contract surfaces; also duplicates what the test tier
+   now does with better failure messages.
+5. *File the finding docs-only (G1/G2 style)* — rejected because this fix needs no
+   protected path: both the byte and the gate live inside approved boundaries, so a
+   docs-only submission would under-deliver what is safely deliverable today.
+   (G1/G2 from the #1590 audit remain pending adoption and stay documented there.)
+
+## 7. Rollback
+
+Single commit, 3 files. `git revert` restores the BOM'd `ruff.toml`, removes the
+gate test and this report; ruff behavior is identical before/after (BOM-tolerant),
+so rollback carries zero functional impact — only the stdlib-parseability and the
+gate are lost.
